      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The Water Lion makes one bite attack against a Large or smaller creature it is grappling. If it hits, the target is swallowed and the grapple ends. The swallowed target is Restrained, fully visible in the Lion's belly, and can't be the target of any jutsu. It must be able to breathe underwater or it begins to drown: it survives rounds equal to its Constitution modifier (minimum 1), then falls unconscious; an unconscious drowning creature takes 6d6 + 6 cold damage at the start of its turn. A creature that's no longer drowning can be woken by another as a bonus action.</p>",
